INSTALLATION:

	1. Uncrunch the LZX archive into your Pfiles directory. Adopt
WallStreet into your pfiles as an AREXX program.
	2. Add Date to your BBS Events to run every day. (also AREXX)
What time you have it run really doesn't matter.
	3. If you want to reward your wealthiest player then add TimeAward
to your sys.welcome file. When a caller calls the first time of the day he 
will be given 30 minutes of extra time online. This time disappears if not 
used during the first call of the day. In your sys.welcome file the line 
should read;
        4.  Added byte credit awards to the monthly winner. The value of 
these credits can be adjusted in the timeaward file to suit your bbs needs. 
Of course this could be a good motivator for callers to play if they need 
credits. If your BBS does not work with byte credits the award can be changed 
to another category using the correct long getuser command and changing the 
ANSI screen to reflect this. To remove this option remove the PZE function 
with a text editor and change line 17 in timeaward to read "then exit". Also 
you will need to use the OLDINTRO ansi in place of the INTRO file by renaming 
it.

      {#0Pfiles/Stocks/TimeAward}
      ^ 
      | This is a control Q

NOTE: All files should be in pfiles/stocks directory!


